    <Folder>
      <name>Intelligence Summary</name>
      <Placemark>
        <name>AI Council Assessment</name>
        <styleUrl>#intel</styleUrl>
        <description>The Western Pacific region continues to be a focal point for naval activities, with the USS Abraham Lincoln Carrier Strike Group arriving in Guam, and the ongoing development of autonomous aircraft mission planning. The U.S. Navy is also demonstrating its commitment to maintaining and modernizing its naval assets, as evidenced by the maintenance availability for the USS Wichita (LCS-13). Additionally, the U.S. has been actively engaged in maritime security operations, including the transfer of a patrol vessel to the Philippines, highlighting the importance of regional stability and security.</description>
        <Point>
          <coordinates>0,0,0</coordinates>
        </Point>
      </Placemark>
